# 1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE

ShortsPilot is a YouTube Shorts automation SaaS.

Its primary purpose is to let users upload multiple different videos and automatically publish six YouTube Shorts every day to their connected YouTube channels.

The application must:

1. Allow users to register and log in.
2. Connect a real YouTube channel using Google OAuth 2.0.
3. Upload multiple Shorts videos in bulk.
4. Apply the same default title, description, and hashtags to every video.
5. Maintain six upcoming scheduled Shorts.
6. Automatically schedule replacement videos when scheduled Shorts are successfully published.
7. Publish videos automatically using the official YouTube Data API v3.
8. Store all data persistently in Firebase.
9. Continue operating when users close their browser or shut down their computers.
10. Display publishing history, queue status, and errors.

The videos must remain different. Their metadata should remain identical unless a user explicitly overrides individual video metadata.

